To draw a chessboard in LaTeX based on a FEN (Forsyth-Edwards Notation) string, you will need to use the `chessboard` package, which provides commands for drawing chessboards and placing pieces. Here is an example code that includes all the required commands and packages:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chessboard} % package for drawing chessboards

\begin{document}

% Define the FEN string
\def\FEN{rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq}

% Draw the chessboard with the given FEN
\makebox[0pt][c]{% use a zero-width box to center the chessboard vertically
  \chessboard[\FEN]
}

% Add labels for the file and rank numbers
\foreach \rank in {1,...,8} {
  \node[anchor=north] at (\rank-1,-0.5) {\rank};
}
\foreach \file in {a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h} {
  \node[anchor=east] at (-0.5,\file) {\file};
}

\end{document}
```

